{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"finitely presented module finitely presented module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md","fileName":"Finitely Presented Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Finitely Presented Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Projective Flat and Injective Modules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Local Criterion for Projectivity","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"finitely presented module finitely presented module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md","fileName":"Finitely Presented Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Finitely Presented Module","heading":"Finitely Presented Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A module is finitely presented when it is generated by finitely many elements and the relations among a finite generating set are themselves finitely generated. Equivalently, it has an exact presentation Rᵐ → Rⁿ → M → 0 with finite m and n.\n\nFinite presentation is stronger than finite generation. It is the finiteness condition needed for a reliable [[Local Criterion for Projectivity]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Local Criterion for Projectivity","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Finitely Presented Module.md","sourceType":"markdown